                <pb facs="0629" n="541" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg541"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1794: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Geneva</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-06-01T13:00:00-04:00">June 1, 1933—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>111. Your 194, June 1, 10 a.m. Colonel Arthur W. Brown, Judge Advocate General’s
                    Department, will report in Washington tomorrow. He will be made available
                    immediately for duty on League Commission. Department presumes he will be
                    appointed by the League as was General McCoy.</p>
                <p>Colombian Minister today advised that Spanish member of Commission will arrive at
                    Puerto Colombia June 15, and was anxious that American member arrive on the same
                    date. As soon as Brown is appointed by the League wire at once full particulars
                    regarding their desires for his movements.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
